[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3196785122","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109735#issuecomment-3196785122","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109735","id":3196785122,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6-ixHi","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-18T13:11:19Z","updated_at":"2025-08-18T13:17:44Z","body":"> And seeing as how there have been no reports about this `!doc->class_list.has(edited_class)` error being emitted alongside the `Can't update documentation` error, it would seem to me like these more random one-off `Can't update documentation` errors are likely caused by some harmless race condition that's presumably a non-issue thanks to stuff like the `EditorHelp::_wait_for_thread` call seen in the code above.\r\n\r\nThe moment I opened this pull request I realized that you of course would never see this `!doc->class_list.has(edited_class)` error since we would early-return from `ScriptEditor::update_doc` thanks to the error-checking that's now removed.\r\n\r\nEither way, the now removed error-checking is clearly redundant, and it's possible that the `EditorHelp::_wait_for_thread` call in `EditorHelp::update_doc` does in fact resolve this somehow, but this definitely needs to be tested by someone who can reproduce this error more reliably than I can.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3196785122/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3201242022","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109735#issuecomment-3201242022","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109735","id":3201242022,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6-zxOm","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-19T15:32:19Z","updated_at":"2025-08-19T15:32:19Z","body":"Thanks!","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3201242022/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"l